![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

This method lacks a `catch` block to handle unexpected errors (such as `localStorage` quota exceeded or network failures during saving). If an error is thrown, `this.isSaving` is reset in `finally`, but `this.vaultStatus` remains stuck on `'Saving...'` or the error is unhandled. Adding a `catch` block improves robustness. Additionally, we should use `$state.snapshot` for `this.spec` and `this.textOutput` to pass clean, non-reactive objects to the storage adapter.

```typescript
	saveToVault = async (): Promise<void> => {
		if (this.isSaving) return;
		if (!this.owner || !this.textOutput) {
			this.vaultStatus = 'Session is still connecting. Try again in a moment.';
			return;
		}
		this.isSaving = true;
		this.vaultStatus = 'Saving...';
		const creationId = this.generateCreationId();
		const storedImages = this.images.map((image) => ({
			b64: image.encoding === 'base64' ? image.data : this.encodeBase64(image.data)
		}));
		try {
			const result = await creationStoreAdapter.saveCreation({
				record: {
					id: creationId,
					createdAtISO: new Date().toISOString(),
					intent: $state.snapshot(this.spec),
					assembledPrompt: this.assembledPrompt || this.textOutput.quote,
					studioText: this.textOutput ? $state.snapshot(this.textOutput) : undefined,
					revisedPrompt: this.revisedPrompt || undefined,
					images: storedImages.length > 0 ? storedImages : undefined,
					violations: this.violations,
					fixesApplied: this.recommendedFixes.map((fix) => fix.code),
					authContext: this.authContext ?? undefined,
					owner: this.owner
				}
			});
			this.vaultStatus = result.ok ? 'Saved to the quote vault.' : result.error.message;
			await this.refreshCreations();
		} catch (error) {
			this.vaultStatus = error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to save to vault.';
		} finally {
			this.isSaving = false;
		}
	};
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In Svelte 5, passing reactive `$state` proxies directly to external adapters or storage can lead to unexpected reactivity tracking, memory leaks, or serialization issues. Using `$state.snapshot` ensures a clean, non-reactive plain JavaScript object is passed.

```suggestion
			await creationStoreAdapter.saveDraft({
				draft: {
					updatedAtISO: new Date().toISOString(),
					intent: $state.snapshot(this.spec),
					chatMessage: this.evidence.trim().length > 0 ? this.evidence : undefined,
					studioText: this.textOutput ? $state.snapshot(this.textOutput) : undefined
				}
			});
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Passing the reactive `this.spec` proxy to the validation adapter can trigger unnecessary reactive reads during schema validation. Using `$state.snapshot` prevents this.

```suggestion
	private async validateSpec(): Promise<boolean> {
		const validation = await specValidationAdapter.validate({ spec: $state.snapshot(this.spec) });
		this.validationIssues = validation.issues;
		return validation.ok;
	}
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Since `dedication` is bound using Svelte's two-way binding (`bind:value={studio.dedication}`), Svelte automatically updates `this.dedication` when the input changes. Manually reading `event.currentTarget.value` and assigning it is redundant and can be safely removed.

```typescript
	handleDedicationInput = (): void => {
		this.spec = { ...this.spec, dedication: this.currentDedication() };
		void this.validateSpec();
		void this.saveDraft();
	};
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Currently, `this.isTextWorking` is set to `true` before validating `safeEvidence`. If `safeEvidence` is empty, the method returns early, briefly flashing the loading state and clearing statuses unnecessarily. Moving the validation check before setting `this.isTextWorking = true` improves UX and code cleanliness. Additionally, we should use `$state.snapshot(this.voice)` to pass a clean, non-reactive copy of the voice settings to the API payload.

```typescript
		this.textError = '';
		this.copyStatus = '';
		this.vaultStatus = '';

		const trimmedEvidence = this.evidence.trim();
		const safeEvidence =
			trimmedEvidence.length > 0 || this.activeMode.toolId === 'random_meechie'
				? trimmedEvidence || 'Random Meechie line request.'
				: '';
		if (!safeEvidence) {
			this.textError = 'Meechie needs a few facts before she can call it.';
			return;
		}

		this.isTextWorking = true;
		try {
			const payload = await postJson('/api/meechie-studio-text', {
				actionId: action.aiAction,
				modeId: this.activeMode.id,
				modeLabel: this.activeMode.label,
				themeLabel: this.activeTheme.label,
				evidence: safeEvidence,
				dedication: this.currentDedication(),
				voice: $state.snapshot(this.voice),
				currentText: this.currentTextPayload()
			});
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Passing the reactive `this.spec` proxy to `postJson` can be avoided by using `$state.snapshot` to ensure a clean, plain object is serialized.

```suggestion
			const payload = await postJson('/api/generate', {
				spec: $state.snapshot(this.spec),
				styleHint: this.currentStyleHint()
			});
```
